/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/T (In May 2024, the U.S. Department of Commerce and the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration announced the new national Center for Heat Resilient Communities[25]. This Center will assist communities across the US, including Tucson, with research, expertise, and actionable policies needed to effectively manage and mitigate extreme heat. This initiative supports Tucson's efforts to create a more livable and equitable Tucson community. Congratulations to the University of Arizona and renowned researchers Ladd Keith, Stephanie Carroll, Laura Bakkensen, and Heidi Brown for being part of this amazing new Center! )
/E (In May 2024, the U.S. Department of Commerce and the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration announced the new national Center for Heat Resilient Communities[25]. This Center will assist communities across the US, including Tucson, with research, expertise, and actionable policies needed to effectively manage and mitigate extreme heat. This initiative supports Tucson's efforts to create a more livable and equitable Tucson community. Congratulations to the University of Arizona and renowned researchers Ladd Keith, Stephanie Carroll, Laura Bakkensen, and Heidi Brown for being part of this amazing new Center! )
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [2 3]
>>
